_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.09717916783200323,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.0560997175970539,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":100.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.019751608559030374,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":67.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.01746,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":11.6,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Jackson Financial Inc., through its subsidiaries, provides suite of annuities to retail investors in the United States. It operates through three segments: Retail Annuities, Institutional Products, and Closed Life and Annuity Blocks. The Retail Annuities segment offers various retirement income and savings products, including variable, fixed index, fixed, and payout annuities, as well as registered index-linked annuities and lifetime income solutions. The Institutional Products segment provides traditional guaranteed investment contracts; funding agreements backed by commercial paper; funding agreements comprising agreements issued in conjunction with its participation in the U.S. federal home loan bank program; and medium-term funding agreement-backed notes. The Closed Life and Annuity Blocks segment offers various protection products, such as whole life, universal life, variable universal life, and term life insurance products, as well as fixed, fixed index, and payout annuities. The company also provides investment management services. It sells its products through a distribution network that includes independent broker-dealers, wirehouses, regional broker-dealers, banks, independent registered investment advisors, third-party platforms, and insurance agents. The company was formerly known as Brooke (Holdco1) Inc. and changed its name to Jackson Financial Inc. in July 2020. Jackson Financial Inc. was incorporated in 2006 and is headquartered in Lansing, Michigan.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Don Wayne Cummings | CEO, President & Director | Age 61 | Compensation: $2.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $2.2M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue falling 7%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $43K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Jackson Financial Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $9.2B market cap on $6.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -23% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 22% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 13-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","On the balance sheet, thin -0.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 9.7% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 184% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.8424972161686433},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 29% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 57/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Learn Why The Bull Case For Jackson Financial (JXN) Could Change Following Earnings And Dividends","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nyse-jxn/jackson-financial/news/learn-why-the-bull-case-for-jackson-financial-jxn-could-chan-1","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794483351.082,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.816,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","dividend"]},{"title":"Avoiding Lag: Real-Time Signals in (JXN) Movement","source":"news.